# An embedded module is compiled into the binary and it lives in its own
# filesystem, which is rooted at its own directory. As a result, its main file
# is found at /main.mcl in that filesystem, and there is usually no such file on
# the local disk. If we ever lose track of which filesystem a source file came
# from, then reading it back errors, and the format check of any program which
# imports an embedded module breaks. Keep an embedded import in the tests.
import "embedded/provisioner"
$x=42
